MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #53's fetchAll looped `page=N` against an endpoint whose pagination is
cursor-based (pagination.next) with no `page` query param: the API ignored
it, page 1 refetched forever, and deploy jobs hung in env-sync until
cancelled. The 9a71149ed revert stopped the hang but a single GET silently
truncates once a project outgrows the default page size — the exact
duplicate-blindness that left stale [development]-only copies undetected
during the 2026-11-12 outage.

Fix: single GET first (what Vercel's own CLI does — get-env-records.ts
does not paginate), then follow pagination.next ONLY when the API returns
one, guarded by a hard page cap (10) and id-dedup so a non-advancing
cursor terminates immediately instead of hanging the deploy.

Also tags the report's untagged code fence (MD040) that 88c8a44db
reintroduced when restoring the pre-5c95d4251 report text.

Co-authored-by: Z User <z@container>
