From 8d2008345cd2b04080e72069fd795f33b79e81f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: afawzy886619888866-cloud <a.fawzy886619888866@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:57:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deps): bump follow-redirects to >=1.16.2 and glob to
 >=14.0.2 (updated advisories) (#61)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The follow-redirects and glob advisories moved after #60 landed: the
follow-redirects fix is now 1.16.2+ (resolves 1.16.3) and glob's is 14.0.2+
(resolves 14.0.6). Floors updated accordingly.

The remaining 2 deepmerge [low] alerts (CVE-2026-93753, prototype
poisoning in mergeObject) cover every 4.2.0-4.3.1 release with NO patched
version published — not actionable until upstream ships a fix. deepmerge
is a dev-tooling transitive here (no app imports), so exposure is limited.

Co-authored-by: Z User <z@container>
