The 3-way viewing dispatch (CEO / Team Leader / Sales Advisor) read
TELEGRAM_*_CHAT_ID env vars that could only be discovered AFTER each
stakeholder messaged the bot once — the capture path was 'operator reads
the /start reply, pastes the id into GitHub secrets, redeploys', which
never happened. The dispatch has therefore honestly skipped all three
roles since it shipped (2026-11-12).

This closes the loop end-to-end, database-first:

  · migration 044: public.telegram_role_chats — one row per staff ROLE
    (chat id, display name, registrant user id, verified, last_tested_at),
    staff-only read, service-role writes, Realtime-streamed (037 pattern).
  · /staffsetup <role> (bot): a staff operator self-registers THEIR chat
    in one message — gated fail-closed by TELEGRAM_STAFF_USER_IDS; the
    confirmation send doubles as verification. /staffstatus lists lanes.
  · lib/server/telegram-role-chats: resolution per role — env override
    (ops escape hatch) → telegram_role_chats → honest skip. Never throws:
    missing table / DB outage degrade to env-only, so the visitor-facing
    201 of /api/viewing-requests stays untouchable.
  · /api/viewing-requests + /api/inquiries sales lane now resolve through
    it (response shape unchanged: same role labels, same delivered flags).
  · /api/admin/telegram-role-chats: GET lane status (source: env|database|
    none) + POST verify test-send with verified/last_tested_at stamping.
  · env-sync: TELEGRAM_{CEO,TEAM_LEADER,SALES_ADVISOR,SALES_REP,ADMIN}_
    CHAT_ID + TELEGRAM_STAFF_USER_IDS (all optional; unset roles skip
    honestly, as today).

Tests: 18 new (resolver order/degradation, staffsetup fail-closed gates,
authorized registration, honest failure reporting) + adjacent suites
122/122 green. Env-only deployments behave exactly as before.

